{"name":"Grass","hex":"#5cac2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A group of languages spoken in Papua New Guinea."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A township in Spencer County, Indiana, United States, named after pioneer settler Daniel Grass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Green Long Legged Fly on Leaf","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg/500px-Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg","ratio":1.2064631956912029,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Long_Legged_Fly_on_Leaf.jpg","share":0.834375},{"title":"Green Colour","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Green_Colour.jpg/500px-Green_Colour.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Colour.jpg","share":0.3025},{"title":"India - Varanasi green peas - 2714","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/India_-_Varanasi_green_peas_-_2714.jpg/500px-India_-_Varanasi_green_peas_-_2714.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_-_Varanasi_green_peas_-_2714.jpg","share":0.083125},{"title":"Lijsterbes (Sorbus). 31-03-2024 (d.j.b.) 02","image":"https://thumb.wikimed